  "id": "child-psychotherapy",
  "term": "child psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Child psychotherapy is a form of therapy with children that can use pretend play as part of the therapeutic process, especially in psychodynamic work. In the supplied source, it is described as helping attachment-traumatised children use imagination and metaphor so they can express hidden trauma-related experiences and move toward mentalisation.",
